{"name":"Little Dipper","hex":"#e4e6ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Little Dipper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A bright circumpolar asterism of the northern sky, said to resemble a ladle or cart. It is part of the constellation Ursa Minor and includes the northern pole star Polaris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Little_Dipper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Little Dipper (Six Flags Great America)","blocks":[{"text":"Little Dipper is a wooden roller coaster located at Six Flags Great America in Gurnee, Illinois. It was built in 1950 at Kiddieland Amusement Park in Melrose Park, Illinois. When the park closed in 2009, Six Flags Great America purchased the ride at an auction. The ride was relocated and reopened on May 27, 2010."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Little_Dipper_May-2010.jpg/330px-Little_Dipper_May-2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Dipper_(Six_Flags_Great_America)","wikidata":"Q6649788"},{"title":"Little Dipper (Memphis Kiddie Park)","blocks":[{"text":"Little Dipper is a junior steel roller coaster located at Memphis Kiddie Park in Brooklyn, Ohio."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/The_Little_Dipper_sign_and_lift%2C_Little_Dipper%2C_May_2016_-_ThrillZing.jpg/330px-The_Little_Dipper_sign_and_lift%2C_Little_Dipper%2C_May_2016_-_ThrillZing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Dipper_(Memphis_Kiddie_Park)","wikidata":"Q6649785"},{"title":"Ursa Minor","blocks":[{"text":"Ursa Minor, also known as the Little Bear, is a constellation located in the far northern sky. As with the Great Bear, the tail of the Little Bear may also be seen as the handle of a ladle, hence the North American name, Little Dipper: seven stars with four in its bowl like its partner the Big Dipper. Ursa Minor was one of the 48 constellations listed by the 2nd-century astronomer Ptolemy, and remains one of the 88 modern constellations. Ursa Minor has traditionally been important for navigation, particularly by mariners, because of Polaris being the north pole star."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Ursa_Minor_IAU.svg/330px-Ursa_Minor_IAU.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursa_Minor","wikidata":"Q10478"},{"title":"Dipper","blocks":[{"text":"Dippers are members of the genus Cinclus in the bird family Cinclidae, so-called because of their bobbing or dipping movements. They are unique among passerines for their ability to dive and swim underwater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Cinclus_mexicanus_FWS.jpg/330px-Cinclus_mexicanus_FWS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dipper","wikidata":"Q192575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Little_Dipper_corner.jpg/500px-Little_Dipper_corner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Little_Dipper_corner.jpg/500px-Little_Dipper_corner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The ride in 2008","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittle_Dipper_corner.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg/500px-Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg/1280px-Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg/500px-Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ursa Minor, with Draco looping around it, as depicted in Urania's Mirror,[5] a set of constellation maps published in London c. 1825","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASidney_Hall_-_Urania's_Mirror_-_Draco_and_Ursa_Minor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg/500px-Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg/1280px-Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg/500px-Book_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ursa Minor as depicted in The Book of Fixed Stars, ca. 1009-1010. Unlike in western representations, the bear is drawn with its tail drooping down.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABook_of_the_Fixed_Stars_Auv0043_ursa_minor_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Ursa_Minor_%28Annotated%29_%28ursa-minor-ann%29.jpg/500px-Ursa_Minor_%28Annotated%29_%28ursa-minor-ann%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Ursa_Minor_%28Annotated%29_%28ursa-minor-ann%29.jpg/1280px-Ursa_Minor_%28Annotated%29_%28ursa-minor-ann%29.jpg?utm